      "body": "## Overview\n\nRegression test for the scattered-head (BHLNC) case of `MooncakeStoreConnector`, the bug in #64117. The code fix landed in #63513, which separated `block_stride` from `block_len`; this PR pins that behaviour for layouts where a head's blocks are interleaved with other heads' and layers' pages, which #63513's own tests (padding on a layer-outermost buffer) do not exercise.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Under a BHLNC-shaped tensor, descriptor sizes equal the dense per-head extent, not the block stride.\n- For every physical block, every descriptor lies inside the registered storage, so a transfer can never run past the allocation, including from the last block.\n- A byte round trip of a middle block and of the last block restores the block and leaves neighbouring layers and the adjacent block untouched.\n\n## Validation\n\n`tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_mooncake_store_layout.py::test_rank_local_scattered_heads_transfer_dense_extent_only[1|2]`: passes on `main` (after #63513); fails on `main` before #63513 with `sizes == [block_stride] * heads`. The rest of the file is unchanged.\n\n## Details\n\nA per-layer view under BHLNC has shape `(B, H, N, C)` and strides `(H·L·N·C, L·N·C, C, 1)`: `head_cache[0]` is dense (`N·C` elements) while `head_cache.stride(0)` spans the whole block. The test builds that tensor from a `(B, H, L, N, C)` buffer, registers one layer's view, and checks descriptors and a round trip with bystander data modified in between. No change to connector code.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
